#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:2 1f84e99da3a04fd4ac34bf1b8e767c36
msgid "Removing a library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:4 1bff5fb0ca634f03b5673f27909098a8
msgid ""
"Removing a library takes it out of ``device.conf``, stops its daemons, "
"and leaves its tapes on disk unless you ask for them to be deleted too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:12 88d2188f0ae74fb3a571c7ab55cb1463
msgid "Before you do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:14 88c732c59ba1479ca7a0301274a7dc91
msgid ""
"**Is anything using it?** A library exported over iSCSI may be mounted by"
" another machine. Remove the export first (:doc:`../using/iscsi`), or "
"that machine keeps a target that points at nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:18 d41badb9d18440b8af7542538163af80
msgid ""
"**Is a tape in a drive?** Removal refuses while a drive holds one - put "
"it back in its slot first, or pass ``--force``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:21 1d29e6b6dd1f466e8c21298a727c4c59
msgid ""
"**Do you want the tapes?** By default they stay on disk, and can be put "
"into another library later with ``tape adopt`` (:doc:`../tapes/adopt`). "
"That is usually what you want: they are data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:26 73f4db7be7f447aa8fa37adea20718ed
msgid "In the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:28 e420d0cfed1a49768b338bb2db5740b3
msgid ""
"The **Remove** button on the library page, or **Libraries → Remove**. You"
" are asked to confirm, and told what will happen to the tapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:31 f5f59ca8e01e4485ac0059876c5c8c50
msgid "Removing a library, and what happens to its tapes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:36 c5ab2545933d4b3c94057fc4749868f7
msgid "From the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:49 49bc165195ab4afe9fd052399f25a6a9
msgid "Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:49 d4e48b9544944b228186b377c31721a9
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:51 6dbe69f8b8044fb98290a3c5dcf97403
msgid "``--remove-media``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:51 e0f649b6af2f427198885dde2bf9e65c
msgid "Delete the tape files too. Not reversible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:52 a199b7b8ae364af88f5943e4439c79e4
msgid "``--force``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:52 d7e877e531fb46898784324a826db15b
msgid "Delete even with a tape loaded in a drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:56 344612412c024c7f9187f064db9e1c90
msgid "What is left behind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:58 81d8f42b2cc34a0f855bb4218e37236d
msgid ""
"Without ``--remove-media``, the tape directories stay under "
"``/opt/mhvtl`` and no library lists them. They are *orphans*, and the "
"console knows it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/remove.rst:72 697c2898e3c44acfbbf0fe3e634ecff3
msgid ""
"Orphans are never cleaned up automatically, because they are data. To "
"take one back into a library, see :doc:`../tapes/adopt`."
msgstr ""

